{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And I spoke to you at that time, saying</b> — before HaShem said to us at Horev, \"You have dwelt long enough at this mountain,\" according to the opinion of those who say that Jethro came before the giving of the Torah, the meaning of <b>at that time</b> is when we were dwelling at Horev. But he mentioned this here to say: behold, we received the Torah, and there were appointed over you judges and officers to judge and govern you, and behold, we were prepared and ready to enter the land, and we journeyed from Horev to our banners together with our judges and our elders, and you all drew near to me with your wise men and your leaders, and you requested spies — and the matter was spoiled."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:43:44.250054933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}